            <ArticleTitle>Ruthenium(II)-Catalyzed Synthesis of Spirobenzofuranones by a Decarbonylative Annulation Reaction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>456-460</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/anie.201710049</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The first decarbonylative insertion of an alkyne through C-H/C-C activation of six-membered compounds is reported. The Ru-catalyzed reaction of 3-hydroxy-2-phenyl-chromones with alkynes works most efficiently in the presence of the ligand PPh3 to provide spiro-indenebenzofuranones. Unlike previously reported metal-catalyzed decarbonylative annulation reactions, in the present decarbonylative annulation reaction, the annulation occurs before extrusion of carbon monoxide.</AbstractText>
